    "title": "'Love Island USA' Urges Viewers To \"Keep It Kind\" Ahead Of Season 8: \"The Villa Runs On Good Vibes\" - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Glenn Garner ,\n1 hours ago As a new group of bombshells prepares to enter the Villa, Love Island USA is reminding viewers to keep it cool on social media.\n‘Love Island USA’ Renewed For Season 8 At Peacock; Premiere Date Set\nOn Wednesday, the Peacock reality dating show released a statement on social media asking viewers to “keep it kind, keep it positive” toward the cast as the streaming platform prepares to debut Season 8 of the Ariana Madix-hosted spin-off of the British series on June 2.\n“The Villa runs on good vibes, and so does this community,” a spokesperson for the show wrote in the statement . “We love seeing your reactions, opinions, and debates, but everyone deserves to feel safe and respected.”\nThey added, “This is a space for fun, not negativity – so keep it kind, keep it positive, and remember: this is LOVE Island !”\n‘Love Island USA’s Ariana Madix On Her Evolution As Host & What She’s Looking Forward To In Season 8 – Contenders TV\nLast summer, Love Island USA had to remind fans that the contestants are “ real people ” in another online statement amid Season 7.\nOn an episode of the weekly chat series Love Island USA: Aftersun , Madix also asked fans to give Islanders grace “before you just hop online and start being absolutely atrocious” to the participants.\nAfter Season 7 became Peacock’s most-watched original season , Love Island USA was renewed for Season 8 in March.\nPeacock Launches 'Law & Order: Clue Hunter' Mobile Game",
